WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.190
- Hi guys, I'm Noah Centineo,
I'm here at BuzzFeed.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.554
I'm gonna be telling you
about my first experiences.

00:00:06.554 --> 00:00:10.280
(upbeat funk music)

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.740
All right, well, I'm
just gonna dive right in.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.980
First cellphone.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.070
Okay, so my parents were never on board

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.220
with the idea that of
us having cellphones,

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.600
but I was lucky because when I was 11,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.550
I went a performing arts school

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.420
that was really far away
from where we lived,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.540
so, not really far away,
but far enough away

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.760
that I had to take the train
to school, public transit,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.980
so they bought me a Verizon Chocolate.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.940
You could slide it up and you could text,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.929
or you slide it back down

00:00:35.929 --> 00:00:39.920
and it had little touch tones
on it, it was fantastic.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:40.890
First cellphone.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.493
First AIM account name, ah.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.319
Oh, God, what was my
first AIM account name?

00:00:48.319 --> 00:00:51.319
(crickets chirping)

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.920
No, noahgc@aol.com.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.753
I used to love that.

00:00:55.753 --> 00:00:57.680
That's where I used to
get all my music from,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.350
the top 10, top five.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.750
I remember Pon De Replay was
on that and like One, Two Step

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.880
and they put the videos up

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.030
and we were like, "Oh, it was so cool."

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.570
Yup, I think Hilary Duff was
on that all the time as well.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.240
Best first date?

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.070
So this was when I lived at The W.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.590
The W Hotel resident side
has a really cool rooftop.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.330
Sweet pool, big W.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.090
She'd come over late afternoon

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.520
sometime close to sunset or just before

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.150
and I said bring a book and we traded.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.560
I gave her Celestine Prophecy

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.950
and she gave me You Are
The One by Kute Blackson

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.140
and we read for like three hours.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.650
I love being sentimental
and remembering things,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.020
it's likes I literally am a sentimentalist

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.610
and that's all I do so this is fantastic.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.510
First pet?

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.810
Oh, I think it was a
rabbit named Princess.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.540
Yeah, and then we got a dog
and the dog ate the rabbit,

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.650
(laughs)
(record scratches)

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.050
and that was the end of the first pet,

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.138
it was the first death I
had ever really experienced

00:02:03.138 --> 00:02:06.120
was the first pet. (laughs)

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.273
This is morbid.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.550
We're out.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:11.383
Okay, last one.

00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:13.270
First time realizing you were famous?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.730
I was 15 years old, I had
just moved to Los Angeles,

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:21.990
I was at the AMC Movie Theater
in Century City with my mom.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.380
We were walking through the lobby

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.367
and these girls came
up to me and they said,

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.637
"Are you Dallas from Austin &amp; Ally,

00:02:29.637 --> 00:02:32.327
"do you play the cellphone
accessory cart guy?"

00:02:32.327 --> 00:02:37.070
And I was like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah,"

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.700
and they were like, "Can we
have a picture with you?"

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.200
And I was like, "Yeah, of
course, like sure, thank you,"

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.460
and we took pictures

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.760
and my mom was kind of just
standing there and beaming

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.753
and I was like dang.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.810
Dang.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.020
Alright guys, my name's Noah Centineo.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.460
You can check out some of the stuff

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.760
that's coming out on Netflix,
Sierra Burgess Is A Loser

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.070
and To All The Boys I
Loved Before, please do it.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.010
We're here at Buzzfeed,
that's all my time with you,

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.637
I love you guys so much,
thank you for tuning it,

00:03:03.637 --> 00:03:06.935
I hope to be back here and
see you guys very soon.

00:03:06.935 --> 00:03:08.687
Deuces.

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:10.996
(laughs)
- [Crew Member] Great.

00:03:10.996 --> 00:03:13.496
(light music)

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.851
(squeaking)

